 ## Aircraft inputs
 
-Above the table:
-
-- **Gallons per Hour** — defaults to `8`; persisted to `localStorage['navaid.aircraft']`.
-- **Taxi and Takeoff (gal)** — startup + taxi + takeoff allowance; defaults to `1.1`. Only added to the total when the origin waypoint matches an entry in `airfields.json` (by name OR by coordinates within ~100 m).
-- The same two figures are in **Settings** (*Gallons per hour*, *Taxi and takeoff (gal)*): one
-  profile, so a change in either place shows in the other at once.
-- **V/S (ft/min)** above the vertical profile — shapes the **departure climb** on the profile and
-  the **TOC** marker on the map; it does **not** change leg times or fuel (those are distance and
-  speed only), and a line under it says so. Also in Settings, the same value.
-- **VOR** — optional reference VOR for Radial/DME columns. It syncs with the toolbar's **VOR ref** selector and persists to `navaid.vorRef`.
+Above the table, the **Aircraft** row:
+
+- **The aircraft** — keyed by its **call sign**: the code the [flight plan form](Submit-Flight-Plan)
+  files after `4X-` (e.g. `CRW`), listed as `4X-CRW (C172)`. The same call sign twice is the same
+  aircraft. Until you give it one it is **No call sign (C172)** — C172 by default.
+- **New aircraft…** asks for a call sign and starts from the figures in use; typing a call sign in
+  **Figures** does the same for the unnamed aircraft, and on one that has a call sign renames it.
+- **Figures** (*Custom figures*) — a popover over the plan, like **Columns** and the departure time,
+  so opening it never makes the plan taller (the plan keeps the size it opened at; nothing in it
+  moves as you type):
+  - **call sign** and **type** — the type is selected for the aircraft: a listed type (C152, C172,
+    PA28, DA40, SR22, AT3, C42, EV97, ULAC) fills its typical manual figures, **Other…** takes any
+    ICAO code;
+  - usable fuel, climb speed, **climb rate** (the rate the vertical profile and the map's **TOC**
+    are drawn with; it does not change leg times or fuel, and a line under it says so), **descent rate**;
+  - **Restore C172 figures**, and **Delete** (asked in the app; the aircraft goes back to having no
+    call sign, with its type).
+
+  Every figure changed while an aircraft is in use is saved into it. Its ✕, Escape (the popover,
+  not the plan) or a tap outside closes it.
+- **Gal/h** and **Taxi + T/O (gal)** — the aircraft's fuel figures. Taxi is added only when the
+  origin waypoint is an airfield in `airfields.json` (by name or within ~100 m). A figure changed
+  from the type's carries a dot, and its tooltip gives the type's value.
+- **VOR**, on its own line under the Aircraft row (it is the route's, not the aircraft's) — optional reference VOR for Radial/DME columns. It syncs with the toolbar's **VOR ref** selector and persists to `navaid.vorRef`.
+
+The descent rate is what the [nav log](Print-and-Export) plans the descent with, unless a rate is
+set in the nav log itself (500 fpm for every listed type).
+
+Stored as `navaid.aircraft` (the aircraft in use) and `navaid.aircraftProfiles` (your own aircraft);
+both sync with Drive when **Sync settings too** is on.
 
